betty white's former assistant pays  tribute to the late actress on what  would have been her 100th birthday you  can't get much better than that kirsten  mikolas betty's longtime assistant  posted this snap of the golden girls  star to betty's official facebook page  monday that's the hollywood legend  posing in a bright green printed top  with white pants gold and white jewelry  and red lipstick and in the caption  kirsten reveals that the picture was  taken on december 20th just 11 days  before her death on new year's eve  kirsten writes that the pick is one of  the last taken of betty i'm just going  along for the ride and having a good  time she adds that at 99 years old betty  was quote radiant and beautiful and as  happy as ever thanks to all of you who  are doing kind things today and every  day to make the world a better place i  think my best wish for the holiday would  be for us all to stop just for a second  and  re-look at our fellow creatures we're  all creatures on this planet and if we  can just be a little kinder to each  other on an individual basis the big  problems will take care of themselves  during et's last interview with betty  leading up to her 99th birthday in 2021  she opened up about how she was feeling  leading up to her big day quote i'm  amazed no seriously i'm the luckiest  broad on two feet to be as healthy as i  am and to feel as good as i do  in fact betty was feeling so good she  was planning on celebrating her  milestone 100th birthday with a  once-in-a-lifetime movie event called  betty white a celebration the film which  premiered on monday betty's birthday was  released in 1500 theaters nationwide i  feel so fortunate to have had as great a  career as i've had for as long as i have  in a press release announcing the  project betty said in part quote who  doesn't love a party this one is gonna  be great the film which takes a look at  her long and successful career includes  interviews with betty behind the scenes  clips of her work and some of her  funniest moments over the years oh it  takes a big woman to forgive somebody  calling her a [ __ ]  the film also includes special tributes  from a-listers who love the late icon  like ryan reynolds tina fey lin-manuel  miranda clint eastwood morgan freeman  jay leno carol burnett jimmy kimmel  valerie bertinelli james corden jennifer  love hewitt and many others i think all  of us truly believe that she would just  live forever i feel so sad that i will  never get to laugh with her again or see  her again  but i also feel so  joyful seeing all the things that people  are putting out about her and how much  they  meant to her and how  you know how she kept us laughing  there's also one last message from betty  to the fans recorded on the same day she  took that final pick the film's producer  opened up to e.t about betty's last  sit-down following the news of her death  december 20th she did a  short little video for us it was kind of  a tribute to her fans that are going to  be with her at the event and it's kind  of a shout out to her fans that she did  10 days before she passed away first of  all she looks amazing she loved getting  glammed up as she calls it and her hair  makeup this is striking and beautiful a  beautiful green  top on bright colored and she was  smiling and really she wanted to thank  her fans sincerely from the bottom of  her heart for all the support over the  years betty died just 17 days short of  her 100th birthday celebration according  to the death certificate obtained by e.t  the beloved actress suffered a stroke  six days before her death in a statement  to et her agent jeff witjos explained  quote i was told that betty passed in  her sleep peacefully without pain to me  this is the most important thing and  brings me comfort as her dear friend  anything else is private to betty and  shortly after she died jeff sat down  with e.t to reflect on betty's impactful  legacy she always called herself the  luckiest old brother i'm a luckiest girl  brought on two feet her legacy would be  bringing people together in many ways  because  young people  older people  great all different races  all love to watch betty white  you can sit in front of the television  and watch whatever she did because it  was funny she never  looked at herself too seriously she had  thoughts about what was going on in the  world  but she kept it to herself  and she brought laughter and happiness  and  a lot of love to a lot of people  [Music]
 

